WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.984
Today is the other way around. Your child takes a whole word, and pulls it apart into its sounds.

2
00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:09.013
Watch first. Then do the same with your child.

3
00:00:09.513 --> 00:00:15.240
You need three counters. Coins, beans or buttons. And say the names of the pictures first.

4
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:21.711
Start with a word of two sounds. Say it slowly, and push one counter into a box for each sound.

5
00:00:22.161 --> 00:00:23.108
The word is up.

6
00:00:25.828 --> 00:00:29.215
Two sounds, two boxes. Now a word of three sounds.

7
00:00:29.665 --> 00:00:30.997
Bed. The word is bed.

8
00:00:34.814 --> 00:00:38.664
The small boxes under each picture show how many sounds to find.

9
00:00:39.114 --> 00:00:47.157
If your child says only the start and then the rest in one piece, that is the usual slip. Say the word again, even more slowly.

10
00:00:47.607 --> 00:00:50.870
Do the first picture together. Your child does the next ones.

11
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.993
For job two, press play on your child's sound track and step away.

12
00:00:55.443 --> 00:01:02.802
Your child touches a dot for each sound. The voice waits, then says the sounds one by one, so your child can check.

13
00:01:03.252 --> 00:01:10.315
At the end, your child says the sounds of three pictures for you. Keep the sound boxes page at the back of the book for later.
